From 6f39477780c14e3f269c97fcbc116a10f2f167f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sanju Abraham <s.abraham@f5.com>
Date: Fri, 29 May 2026 10:25:59 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] security: bump x/crypto v0.49.0 -> v0.52.0, x/net v0.52.0 ->
 v0.55.0, vitest 2.1.0 -> 2.1.9

Fixes the following CVEs flagged by CI:

  golang.org/x/crypto v0.49.0:
    CVE-2026-39830 (9.1), CVE-2026-39831 (9.1), CVE-2026-39832 (9.1),
    CVE-2026-39833 (9.1), CVE-2026-39834 (9.1), CVE-2026-42508 (9.1),
    CVE-2026-46595 (10.0)

  golang.org/x/net v0.52.0:
    CVE-2026-39821 (9.6)

  vitest 2.1.0 (and @vitest/coverage-v8, @vitest/ui):
    CVE-2025-24964 (9.6)

Applied directly to the base source rather than via the f5xc-patches
overlay system because container-image security scans run against the
checked-out base tree before make apply-patches has had a chance to run.
A reference copy of this change set lives under f5xc-patches/security/
for audit purposes.
